  "question": {
    "text": "Three blocks $M_1, M_2, M_3$ having masses $4 \\mathrm{~kg}, 6 \\mathrm{~kg}$ and $10 \\mathrm{~kg}$ respectively are hanging from a smooth pully using rope 1,2 and 3 as shown in figure. The tension in the rope $1, T_1$ when they are moving upward with acceleration of $2 \\mathrm{~ms}^{-2}$ is _____$\\mathrm{N}\\left(\\right.$ if $\\mathrm{g}=10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2$ ).\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/F91sDLyweA6FXrShLDhV2pMG7zWts3EL5WgXun_Zens.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "240",
  "solution": {
    "text": "FBD of $M_1$ :\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/N05qK9mwA7KGvi1eCO3kxzUa-5_iBViHJt3sVZFBc9I.original.fullsize.png\"><br />$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{T}_1-200=(4+6+10) \\times 2 \\\\\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{T}_1=240\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
